\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Remark}
\title{Why the entropy statistics are not interchangeable}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{entropy}

\p{We formulate global and position-level aggregates from Shannon's finite
entropy \citef{shannon1948mathematical}. They average over different random
objects. Selected-token surprisal is a sample statistic, while the other two
are expectations under declared history or position laws.}

\p{A training intervention can raise one quantity while lowering another.
Later claims about exploration or collapse must name the statistic, sampling
law, horizon, and conditioning event.}
